    "question": {
      ":question/id": "95ad7446-13d1-523e-98b0-a7f80d96ac94",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3 t,\\qquad y=t^{2} + 1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\nUse the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, $x(-2)=3 \\left(-2\\right)=-6$.\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $2$ | {{field-3}} |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $5$ |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The missing entry is in the $x$-row under $t=2$. Substitute into $x=3 t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) &=3 \\left(2\\right) \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=-2$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} + 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-2) &=\\left(-2\\right)^{2} + 1 \\\\ &=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing entry is in the $y$-row under $t=0$. Substitute into $y=t^{2} + 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) &=\\left(0\\right)^{2} + 1 \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\n| **$t$** | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $5$ |",
